### Key Findings
- CA2 TeNT silencing → 100% social memory loss, all other memories intact (Hitti 2014)
- RGS14 suppresses LTP via 5 pathways (AC, cAMP, PKA, AMPA, ERK), but KO impairs social memory (Samadi 2023) — CA2 uses mGluR-LTD, not LTP, for social memory storage
- Avpr1b in CA2 (not CA1/CA3): vasopressin/oxytocin from PVN gates plasticity window (Pagani 2015)
- CA2→CA1 silencing: 48% time cells disrupted (149/313), only 15% place cells (MacDonald 2021)
- CA2 ramping cells fire 20-30ms before SWR peak; optogenetic CA2 activation → 3× SWR rate (Oliva 2016)

